309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 267 0 R
/T (Seoul has never been easier to eat your way through. Ranking lists, short videos and map ratings send visitors to the same handful of places, and the lines outside them grow longer every year. But many of the city's best meals happen somewhere else: in a family restaurant that has served one dish since the 1940s, at a dumpling counter by the gate of a market, or in a noodle shop in the basement of an apartment complex.)
/E (Seoul has never been easier to eat your way through. Ranking lists, short videos and map ratings send visitors to the same handful of places, and the lines outside them grow longer every year. But many of the city's best meals happen somewhere else: in a family restaurant that has served one dish since the 1940s, at a dumpling counter by the gate of a market, or in a noodle shop in the basement of an apartment complex.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 267 0 R
/T (This book collects 24 of those places. They were chosen for their stories and for the part they play in their neighborhoods, not for how often they appear online. Some have fed the same families for three generations. Others are small, newer kitchens run by cooks who want to make one thing well. All of them are independent, and all of them are places where locals actually eat.)
/E (This book collects 24 of those places. They were chosen for their stories and for the part they play in their neighborhoods, not for how often they appear online. Some have fed the same families for three generations. Others are small, newer kitchens run by cooks who want to make one thing well. All of them are independent, and all of them are places where locals actually eat.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 267 0 R
/T (Each entry tells the restaurant's story and then gives you what you need to visit: what to order, with the Korean name to show the staff, when to go to avoid the longest lines, and how to get there by subway. The restaurants are grouped into four parts of the city, so you can plan a day around one neighborhood and eat your way across it.)
/E (Each entry tells the restaurant's story and then gives you what you need to visit: what to order, with the Korean name to show the staff, when to go to avoid the longest lines, and how to get there by subway. The restaurants are grouped into four parts of the city, so you can plan a day around one neighborhood and eat your way across it.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
