474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 272 0 R
/T (Tosokchon opened in 1983 in Seochon, the old neighborhood just west of Gyeongbokgung Palace. Its dining rooms run through several connected hanok, so you walk under tiled eaves and across small courtyards to reach your table. The kitchen is known for one dish: a whole young chicken stuffed with glutinous rice and simmered with ginseng, jujube, chestnut, ginkgo and pine nuts until the broth turns thick and nutty. The late President Roh Moo-hyun was a well-known regular, which only added to its fame. On the hottest days of summer, Koreans eat samgyetang to fight the heat, and the line here shows it.)
/E (Tosokchon opened in 1983 in Seochon, the old neighborhood just west of Gyeongbokgung Palace. Its dining rooms run through several connected hanok, so you walk under tiled eaves and across small courtyards to reach your table. The kitchen is known for one dish: a whole young chicken stuffed with glutinous rice and simmered with ginseng, jujube, chestnut, ginkgo and pine nuts until the broth turns thick and nutty. The late President Roh Moo-hyun was a well-known regular, which only added to its fame. On the hottest days of summer, Koreans eat samgyetang to fight the heat, and the line here shows it.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
