500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 273 0 R
/T (Dakhanmari means 'one whole chicken'. The dish grew up in the 1970s around the markets of Dongdaemun, where busy traders and bus travelers shouted the name to order fast. A brass pot of chicken, broth and potatoes is set on a burner at your table and you cook it yourself, dipping each piece in a sauce you mix from chili, soy, vinegar and mustard. Baekbujangjip serves it from its main restaurant near Jonggak, a short walk from Insadong, with a second dining room around the corner for the evening rush. When the chicken is gone, noodles go into the broth to finish.)
/E (Dakhanmari means 'one whole chicken'. The dish grew up in the 1970s around the markets of Dongdaemun, where busy traders and bus travelers shouted the name to order fast. A brass pot of chicken, broth and potatoes is set on a burner at your table and you cook it yourself, dipping each piece in a sauce you mix from chili, soy, vinegar and mustard. Baekbujangjip serves it from its main restaurant near Jonggak, a short walk from Insadong, with a second dining room around the corner for the evening rush. When the chicken is gone, noodles go into the broth to finish.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
