924 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 290 0 R
/T (Shin Woo-gyoung opened her restaurant in 1939, when Koreans could not use the word 'Korea' in a business name, so it was called Hwaseonok. After liberation in 1945 she renamed it Hanilkwan. It moved to Busan during the Korean War, returned to Jongno, and was run by her daughter and then her granddaughters, who brought it back from near closure in the late 1990s. When Jongno was redeveloped in 2008, the main restaurant moved here to Apgujeong. Its Seoul-style bulgogi helped make the dish a household name.)
/E (Shin Woo-gyoung opened her restaurant in 1939, when Koreans could not use the word 'Korea' in a business name, so it was called Hwaseonok. After liberation in 1945 she renamed it Hanilkwan. It moved to Busan during the Korean War, returned to Jongno, and was run by her daughter and then her granddaughters, who brought it back from near closure in the late 1990s. When Jongno was redeveloped in 2008, the main restaurant moved here to Apgujeong. Its Seoul-style bulgogi helped make the dish a household name.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
