976 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 292 0 R
/T (Hulaendeu, a Korean spelling of 'friend', is a tiny kimbap shop in a small shopping arcade among the Apgujeong apartment blocks. It opens at 7 AM, and early risers line up for simple rolls of rice, egg, cucumber, carrot and pickled radish. It has fed the neighborhood for years, and the counter also sells homemade sesame and perilla seed brittle. The flavors are mild and old-fashioned, which is exactly why neighbors keep coming back.)
/E (Hulaendeu, a Korean spelling of 'friend', is a tiny kimbap shop in a small shopping arcade among the Apgujeong apartment blocks. It opens at 7 AM, and early risers line up for simple rolls of rice, egg, cucumber, carrot and pickled radish. It has fed the neighborhood for years, and the counter also sells homemade sesame and perilla seed brittle. The flavors are mild and old-fashioned, which is exactly why neighbors keep coming back.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [5]
>>
