<<
/Title (This book collects 24 of those places. They were chosen for their stories and for the part they play in their neighborhoods, not for how often they appear online. Some have fed the same families for three generations. Others are small, newer kitchens run by cooks who want to make one thing well. All of them are independent, and all of them are places where locals actually eat.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1692 0 R
/Prev 1904 0 R
/Next 2274 0 R
>>
endobj
