<<
/Title (The Eunma Apartments, built at the end of the 1970s, sit at the center of Daechi-dong, the district famous for its after-school academies. In the basement of the complex's shopping arcade, Sanwol has been serving noodle soup for more than thirty years. There are only three dishes: kalguksu \(knife-cut noodles\), sujebi \(hand-torn dough\) or a mix of both, all in a clear anchovy broth. Students, parents and shop owners share the counters, adding spoonfuls of sauce and fresh kimchi.)
