2333 0 obj
<<
/Title (Woo Lae Oak has served Pyongyang-style naengmyeon since 1946, making it one of the oldest restaurants still running in Seoul. The building sits a few steps off Euljiro, an old district of lighting, tool and print shops, and its dining rooms fill every summer with regulars who have been coming for decades. The noodles are made with buckwheat and served in a clear, cold beef broth that tastes plain at first and deeper with every sip. Many tables start with bulgogi on a copper grill and finish with noodles, the classic Korean way to end a meat meal.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2307 0 R
/Prev 2332 0 R
/First 2361 0 R
/Last 2362 0 R
/Count -6
>>
endobj
