2337 0 obj
<<
/Title (In Korea, grilled freshwater eel is eaten for stamina, especially on hot summer days. At Namseoul, the eels wait in freshwater tanks and go onto the grill only after you order, so the meal takes about twenty minutes and is worth the wait. Most of the staff have worked here for more than ten years, and they grill the eel at your table until it turns golden brown. You can have it with a soy-based glaze or simply salted, wrapped in leaves with ginger and garlic.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2308 0 R
/Prev 2336 0 R
