2397 0 obj
<<
/Title (Dakhanmari means 'one whole chicken'. The dish grew up in the 1970s around the markets of Dongdaemun, where busy traders and bus travelers shouted the name to order fast. A brass pot of chicken, broth and potatoes is set on a burner at your table and you cook it yourself, dipping each piece in a sauce you mix from chili, soy, vinegar and mustard. Baekbujangjip serves it from its main restaurant near Jonggak, a short walk from Insadong, with a second dining room around the corner for the evening rush. When the chicken is gone, noodles go into the broth to finish.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2365 0 R
/Prev 2396 0 R
/First 2434 0 R
/Last 2435 0 R
/Count -6
>>
