/Title (Sindang-dong is famous for tteokbokki, but after dark many locals walk a few streets over to Ujeong for chicken feet. Here they are braised until the meat slips off the bone, then coated in a glossy sauce that comes in two strengths: mild and properly spicy. Regulars order one of each and switch between them, cooling down with a pot of the shop's own table-cooked tteokbokki. It stays open until the early hours, which makes it a neighborhood favorite for late dinners and second rounds.)
