2617 0 obj
<<
/Title (Seorae Village is known as Seoul's little France, home to the city's French community and its bakeries and bistros. Seorae Jjukkumi is the village's Korean side: a busy local spot where baby octopus is marinated in a spicy sauce and cooked on a hot iron plate at your table. The octopus picks up a smoky char and stays tender, and it comes with crunchy bean sprouts and greens to cool the heat. Pancakes made with perilla leaves or chives are the usual side.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
